      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg at once is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rises sharply. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? These are common options:\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours (four times daily):** 1,600 mg/day, which is typical for mild to moderate pain.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day, which is often used for inflammatory conditions.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, which is the maximum.\n- **1600 mg/day total:** This may be what was meant, divided into four doses of 400 mg.\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that you really mean 1600 mg four times daily. If you confirm it, I'd want a documented clinical rationale first. I'll enter the order once it's clarified."
      }
